---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TerminalAnimation from '../components/TerminalAnimation';
import HealthTable from '../components/HealthTable.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description="Take back control of your digital life with self-hosted media, photo backups, and private cloud storage."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative pt-12 pb-20 md:pt-24 md:pb-32 overflow-hidden border-b border-border">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center text-center">
      <div class="mb-6 px-3 py-1 border border-border text-xs font-mono text-text-muted tracking-widest uppercase bg-bg-surface/50 backdrop-blur-sm animate-fade-up">
        SYS.INIT // HOMELABBING_V1
      </div>
      
      <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-black tracking-tighter text-text max-w-5xl mx-auto leading-[0.9] animate-fade-up font-display uppercase">
        Own Your Cloud. <br />
        <span class="text-accent">Ditch Subscriptions.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-8 text-base sm:text-lg text-text-muted font-mono max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.1s;">
        Why pay $50+ a month for Netflix, Spotify, Google Photos, and Dropbox when you can host them locally on your own hardware with superior privacy and zero ongoing fees?
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.2s;">
        <a href="/Homelabbing/getting-started" class="btn-primary text-sm">
          Initialize setup
        </a>
        <a href="/Homelabbing/concepts" class="btn-secondary text-sm">
          View architecture
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Terminal Animation Island -->
      <div class="mt-20 w-full max-w-4xl animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.3s;">
        <TerminalAnimation client:load />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Hardware Guide (Brutalist Spec Sheet) -->
  <section class="py-24 border-b border-border bg-bg">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[250px_1fr] gap-8 md:gap-16">
        
        <!-- Left Sidebar Data -->
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-text-muted space-y-8 flex flex-col pt-3 md:border-r md:border-border/50 md:pr-8">
          <div>
            <div class="text-accent mb-2 border-b border-border/50 pb-2">01 // TOPIC</div>
            <div class="uppercase tracking-widest">STARTING A HOMELAB</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-accent mb-2 border-b border-border/50 pb-2">02 // OBJECTIVE</div>
            <div>Self-host applications & maintain data control.</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-accent mb-2 border-b border-border/50 pb-2">03 // STATUS</div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-success rounded-none animate-pulse"></span> SYSTEM NOMINAL</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right Content -->
        <div class="space-y-16">
          
          <!-- Intro -->
          <div class="animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.1s;">
            <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black font-display tracking-tight text-text uppercase mb-6">STARTING A HOMELAB</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed font-mono">
              <p>Homelabbing can be an overwhelming hobby to get started in. Browse places like <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/homelab/" class="text-text hover:text-accent border-b border-border hover:border-accent transition-colors">r/homelab</a> and you will quickly find an abundance of large racks storing rows of computers and networking hardware, along with the odd smaller lab peppered in between. But the great thing about homelabbing is it can be as big, or more importantly, as small as you want.</p>
              <p>A breakdown of hardware options and use cases for starting a self-hosted homelab.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Why -->
          <div class="spec-sheet p-8 border-l-4 border-l-accent bg-bg-surface animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.2s;">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold font-display uppercase tracking-tight text-text mb-6">Why start a homelab?</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-4 font-mono text-sm text-text-muted">
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span class="text-accent opacity-50 shrink-0">[1]</span> <span>Somewhere to learn a technology for work or education. For example, buying a Cisco switch from eBay to study for a networking certification.</span></li>
              <li class="flex gap-4"><span class="text-accent opacity-50 shrink-0">[2]</span> <span>To self host applications, reducing reliance on the cloud or big tech. Replacing Dropbox with Nextcloud, or firing up PiHole to block ads.</span></li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-border/50 text-text-muted text-sm font-mono italic pl-4 border-l-2 border-border">
              "Self-hosting provides direct control over data and a flexible environment to rapidly deploy containerized services."
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Hardware List -->
          <div class="animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.3s;">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-black font-display tracking-tight text-text uppercase mb-8 border-b border-border pb-4">HARDWARE OPTIONS</h2>
            
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4">
              <!-- Item 1 -->
              <div class="spec-sheet p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 hover:border-accent/50 transition-colors">
                <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 font-mono text-sm border-r border-border/50 pr-4">
                  <div class="text-accent mb-2 text-xs">OPT-01</div>
                  <div class="text-text font-bold mb-2 uppercase">Old Computer</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs">COST // $0</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-1">ENERGY // HIGH</div>
                </div>
                <div class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted space-y-2">
                  <p>You may have an old laptop or PC kicking about just waiting to be repurposed. This is the perfect candidate for starting as it’s free.</p>
                  <p>Bonus: built in battery acting as a UPS.</p>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-border/30">
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Docker</span>
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Hypervisor (Proxmox)</span>
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">NAS (Unraid)</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Item 2 -->
              <div class="spec-sheet p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 hover:border-accent/50 transition-colors">
                <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 font-mono text-sm border-r border-border/50 pr-4">
                  <div class="text-accent mb-2 text-xs">OPT-02</div>
                  <div class="text-text font-bold mb-2 uppercase">Raspberry Pi</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs">COST // $15 - $35+</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-1">ENERGY // V.LOW</div>
                </div>
                <div class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted space-y-2">
                  <p>A great low cost option for starting a homelab. It’s a small, but capable, machine with a large community.</p>
                  <p class="text-warning mt-2 inline-block border border-warning/30 px-2 py-1 bg-warning/5">Notice: Don't rely on the Pi to store your only copy of data.</p>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-border/30">
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">PiHole</span>
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Home Assistant</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Item 3 -->
              <div class="spec-sheet p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 hover:border-accent/50 transition-colors">
                <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 font-mono text-sm border-r border-border/50 pr-4">
                  <div class="text-accent mb-2 text-xs">OPT-03</div>
                  <div class="text-text font-bold mb-2 uppercase">NAS Appliance</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs">COST // $250 - $500+</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-1">ENERGY // MED</div>
                </div>
                <div class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted space-y-2">
                  <p>Brands like Synology and Ugreen offer built NAS appliances ready to go out of the box.</p>
                  <p class="text-accent font-bold mt-2">HOWEVER:</p>
                  <p>The true point of homelabbing is that you can build a NAS yourself using an old second-hand PC and some hard drives, giving you complete control and no "brand tax".</p>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-border/30">
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Network Storage</span>
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Media Server</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Item 4 -->
              <div class="spec-sheet p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 hover:border-accent/50 transition-colors">
                <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 font-mono text-sm border-r border-border/50 pr-4">
                  <div class="text-accent mb-2 text-xs">OPT-04</div>
                  <div class="text-text font-bold mb-2 uppercase">Second Hand PC</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs">COST // $50 - $300+</div>
                  <div class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-1">ENERGY // MED-HIGH</div>
                </div>
                <div class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted space-y-2">
                  <p>Similar to the “Old Computer”, but with much more choice. Ex-corporate machines like Dell Optiplex or Lenovo ThinkCentre are perfect.</p>
                  <p>Provides the most flexibility and scale.</p>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-border/30">
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Proxmox</span>
                    <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-bg border border-border text-xs">Arch Linux</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Security & Conclusion -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.4s;">
            <div class="spec-sheet p-6 border-t-2 border-t-warning border-l-0 border-r-0 border-b-0 border border-border bg-bg-surface">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono tracking-tight text-text mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-warning inline-block"></span> SECURITY WARNING
              </h3>
              <p class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
                It’s tempting to expose your new homelab to the internet. But unless you understand the risks and how to mitigate them (firewalls, VPNs, tunnels), you shouldn't. You are opening yourself up to malicious threats.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="spec-sheet p-6 border-t-2 border-t-accent bg-accent/5 border-l-0 border-r-0 border-b-0 border border-border">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono tracking-tight text-accent mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-accent inline-block animate-pulse"></span> CONCLUSION
              </h3>
              <p class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Homelabbing doesn’t have to be about big expensive gear. Start small and explore. <br/><br/>
                <strong class="text-text">Happy homelabbing.</strong>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Concepts Banner -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-bg-surface border-b border-border">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-2 block">Architecture First Foundation</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black font-display uppercase tracking-tight text-text">A Modular Ecosystem & Guide</h2>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm font-mono mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            A modular Docker Compose reference architecture and guide for self-hosted home servers. Designed around understanding core architecture over magic scripts. Conceptual guides cover container networking, volume persistence, reverse proxy routing, and service security.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="/Homelabbing/concepts" class="btn-primary shrink-0 text-sm">
          Browse guides
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Project Audit -->
  <section class="py-24 border-b border-border">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
        <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-2 block">Project Audit</span>
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-black font-display uppercase tracking-tight text-text">State of the Repository</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted font-mono text-sm mt-4">An overview of repository structure, maintainability, and security practices.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="spec-sheet p-8 group transition-colors animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.1s;">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-text mb-3 uppercase">Structure & Organization</h3>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-text-muted leading-relaxed">The project is 100% modular, with heavily commented <code class="text-accent bg-bg px-1 py-0.5 border border-border">stacks/</code> directories. Documentation quality focuses on architecture-first conceptual guides.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-sheet p-8 group transition-colors animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.2s;">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-text mb-3 uppercase">Architecture & Maintainability</h3>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-text-muted leading-relaxed">Employs the <code class="text-accent bg-bg px-1 py-0.5 border border-border">.env.example</code> pattern across all stacks and uses read-only mounts to ensure data safety.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-sheet p-8 group transition-colors animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.3s;">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-text mb-3 uppercase">Security Best Practices</h3>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-text-muted leading-relaxed">Tailscale and Cloudflare options are provided for secure external access without needing port forwarding.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-sheet p-8 border-l-4 border-l-accent bg-accent/5 group transition-colors animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.4s;">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-mono text-accent mb-3 uppercase">Improvement Area</h3>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-text-muted leading-relaxed">Currently, there is an overuse of <code class="text-accent bg-bg/50 px-1 py-0.5 border border-accent/20">:latest</code> image tags in <code class="text-accent bg-bg/50 px-1 py-0.5 border border-accent/20">docker-compose.yml</code> files, which can lead to breaking changes upon auto-updates.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Modular Services Section -->
  <section class="py-24 border-b border-border bg-bg">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end justify-between mb-16 gap-4">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-2 block">Modular Stacks</span>
          <h2 class="text-4xl font-black font-display uppercase tracking-tight text-text">Pick Where You Want to Start</h2>
          <p class="text-text-muted font-mono text-sm mt-4 max-w-2xl">
            Modular Docker stacks organized by function. Each application resides in a dedicated directory.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="/Homelabbing/services" class="text-accent hover:text-text font-mono text-sm flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0 transition-colors border-b border-accent hover:border-text pb-0.5">
          View all stacks
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="my-12 p-2 spec-sheet bg-bg-surface">
        <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/architecture.png`} alt="Detailed architecture diagram showing reverse proxy, modular stacks, and docker services routing" class="w-full h-auto mix-blend-screen opacity-80" />
        <div class="border-t border-border mt-2 pt-2 px-2 pb-1 flex justify-between font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">
          <span>FIG 01 // ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM</span>
          <span>SOURCE: REFERENCE DOCS</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-8">
        {[
          { title: "Main README & Stacks Hub", desc: "Core philosophy and an overview of all modular components in the repository." },
          { title: "Media Server", desc: "Stream media across devices using Jellyfin." },
          { title: "*Arr Stack", desc: "Automated downloads. Uses shared parent directory mounts for zero-copy hardlinking." },
          { title: "Music Server", desc: "Personal music streaming with Navidrome." },
          { title: "Photo Backup", desc: "4-container Google Photos alternative (Immich) with local AI facial recognition." },
          { title: "Book Reader", desc: "Host and read digital manga and ebooks using Kavita." },
          { title: "Cloud Storage", desc: "Self-hosted private cloud storage with Nextcloud." },
          { title: "Home Automation", desc: "Smart home control running on Home Assistant." },
          { title: "Networking", desc: "Includes Tailscale and Cloudflare options for secure external access without port forwarding." }
        ].map((stack, i) => (
          <div class="spec-sheet p-6 group hover:border-accent transition-colors flex flex-col justify-between animate-fade-up" style={`animation-delay: ${0.1 + i * 0.05}s;`}>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold font-mono text-text uppercase mb-2 flex justify-between items-start gap-4">
                {stack.title}
                <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-none bg-success animate-pulse shrink-0 mt-1"></span>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs font-mono text-text-muted leading-relaxed">{stack.desc}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-border/50 text-xs font-mono text-text-muted/50 group-hover:text-accent transition-colors">
              // MODULE {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
        
        <div class="spec-sheet p-6 group hover:border-accent transition-colors lg:col-span-3 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center justify-between gap-6 bg-bg-surface animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.55s;">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold font-mono text-text uppercase mb-2 flex items-center gap-3">
              Full Stack <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-none bg-success animate-pulse"></span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs font-mono text-text-muted leading-relaxed">A complete setup combining all individual stacks together into one massive deployment.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono text-text-muted/50 group-hover:text-accent transition-colors shrink-0">
            // OMEGA MODULE
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Health & Port Reference -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-surface border-b border-border">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
        <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-2 block">Live Monitoring</span>
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-black font-display uppercase tracking-tight text-text">Check All Your Ports in One Command</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          The diagnostic script queries container states across all homelab service endpoints (<code class="text-accent">http://YOUR_SERVER_IP:PORT</code>) and reports container health directly in the terminal.
        </p>
      </div>

      <HealthTable />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Self-Host Banner -->
  <section class="py-32 border-b border-border relative overflow-hidden bg-bg">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-[800px] h-[800px] bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_center,rgba(255,62,0,0.05)_0,transparent_50%)] pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 text-center relative z-10">
      
      <div class="mb-8 font-mono text-xs text-accent tracking-widest uppercase">
        // END OF FILE
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black font-display uppercase tracking-tight text-text">
        Ready to Build Your Private Home Cloud?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted font-mono max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Docker Compose blueprints, environment templates, and architecture guides for self-hosting. For additional community services, explore the <a href="https://www.awesome-homelab.com/" target="_blank" class="text-accent hover:text-text border-b border-accent hover:border-text transition-colors pb-0.5">Awesome-Homelab</a> directory.
      </p>
      
      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/Homelabbing/getting-started" class="btn-primary text-sm">
          Initialize now
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Zamiul-rashid/Homelabbing"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="btn-secondary text-sm"
        >
          Star on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
